#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:6
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:8
msgid "`Send + Sync`"
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:10
msgid "Most types you come across are `Send + Sync`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:12
msgid "`i8`, `f32`, `bool`, `char`, `&str`, ..."
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:13
msgid "`(T1, T2)`, `[T; N]`, `&[T]`, `struct { x: T }`, ..."
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:14
msgid "`String`, `Option<T>`, `Vec<T>`, `Box<T>`, ..."
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:15
msgid "`Arc<T>`: Explicitly thread-safe via atomic reference count."
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:16
msgid "`Mutex<T>`: Explicitly thread-safe via internal locking."
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:17
msgid "`mpsc::Sender<T>`: As of 1.72.0."
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:18
msgid "`AtomicBool`, `AtomicU8`, ...: Uses special atomic instructions."
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:20
msgid ""
"The generic types are typically `Send + Sync` when the type parameters are "
"`Send + Sync`."
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:23
msgid "`Send + !Sync`"
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:25
msgid ""
"These types can be moved to other threads, but they're not thread-safe. "
"Typically because of interior mutability:"
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:28
msgid "`mpsc::Receiver<T>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:29
msgid "`Cell<T>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:30
msgid "`RefCell<T>`"
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:32
msgid "`!Send + Sync`"
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:34
msgid ""
"These types are safe to access (via shared references) from multiple "
"threads, but they cannot be moved to another thread:"
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:37
msgid ""
"`MutexGuard<T>`: Uses OS level primitives which must be deallocated on the "
"thread which created them. However, an already-locked mutex can have its "
"guarded variable read by any thread with which the guard is shared (unless "
"`T` itself is `!Sync`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:42
msgid "`!Send + !Sync`"
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:44
msgid "These types are not thread-safe and cannot be moved to other threads:"
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:46
msgid ""
"`Rc<T>`: each `Rc<T>` has a reference to an `RcBox<T>`, which contains a non-"
"atomic reference count."
msgstr ""

#: src/concurrency/send-sync/examples.md:48
msgid ""
"`*const T`, `*mut T`: Rust assumes raw pointers may have special concurrency "
"considerations."
msgstr ""
